WEBVTT

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.980
<i>Jean and the others washed ashore on a desert island</i>

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.690
<i>where they have started a new life,</i>

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.360
<i>overcoming many difficulties such as famine, drought, sickness,</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.820
<i>Nadia and Jean's first kisses and Nadia's selfishness.</i>

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:45.540
<i>But everything they had created was destroyed by a sudden typhoon.</i>

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.580
<i>Then, to their amazement, a huge island appeared before them.</i>

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.210
<i>While they were exploring the island,</i>

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.170
<i>they encountered Ayerton, Grandis, Sanson and Hanson again.</i>

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.050
<i>Now, everyone is living on the new island together,</i>

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:05.100
<i>but there will always be problems when people gather together.</i>

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:09.400
<i>How long can this peace possibly last?</i>

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.820
No! Please don't go!

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.410
Just a dream?

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:26.870
What's wrong?

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.630
I'm sorry. Did I wake you?

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.210
Did you have a nightmare?

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.800
Yes, I had a dream about him.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.010
I must be the unluckiest woman in the world.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.730
I could say the same thing.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.650
Your situation is much better.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.020
You have a wonderful boyfriend in Jean with you.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.110
But...

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.780
You can see him every morning.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.120
You may consider it natural,

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.240
but it's the most luxurious thing in the world.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.080
My situation is different. Just look at me.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:13.210
I fell in love with someone I shouldn't have loved.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.800
Love isn't always kind.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.880
But I don't want to stay with him all the time.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.970
It's because of this situation.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.310
Someday you'll want him to be with you,

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.980
but he won't necessarily be able to by then.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:36.070
But Grandis, you have lots of men around you now.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.990
What are you doing?

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.070
I had my eyes set on it first.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.530
I thought I was going to eat the last one.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.370
You've eaten a lot already!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.370
Of course! I caught these fish!

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:55.080
I made that fishing rod! I also made the stove it was cooked on!

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.380
What's that?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:06.220
This is what I have to choose from?

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.180
This must be my fate.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.180
No, it isn't!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.730
There are two types of people in this world,

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.440
good people and bad people.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.400
Would you care for some tea?

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.160
Well, which type am l?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.030
If you'll excuse me...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.830
Do you read palms?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.790
No, of course not, but...

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.380
But what?

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:45.590
Luck has been known to change in some cases.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.680
It depends upon the men around you.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.940
What are you talking about? We change our luck by ourselves!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.190
Geez, grown-ups!

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.690
What happened?

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:05.450
They worry too much about too many trivial things.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.280
Everybody's like that.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.740
Not me.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.410
But we need to do it to live.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.160
Do you think so?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.170
Man cannot live alone.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:23.010
There are many obstacles that we must overcome in our society.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:23.510
Jean...

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.680
Do you always use that toothbrush?

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.640
Yes, I do.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.220
I use it too.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.990
Will you move aside?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:50.530
That hurt.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.620
Don't enter my territory then!

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.710
Who settled this land?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.580
It was settled a long time ago.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:02.590
From what time, what day, what month, what year?

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:12.050
It was settled 999,999,999,999,999 years ago!

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:15.470
Who settled it then? Dinosaurs?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.440
I settled it!

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.150
Really? But don't you live by yourself?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:26.820
Shut up! This is the border! Don't go beyond this!

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.400
How about in the air?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:31.120
Not in the air either!

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.000
What's the matter with those two?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.210
Are they fighting?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.670
Just like children.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.670
How childish.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.180
You've got to do something, Grandis.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.890
I have no luck with men.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.820
Captain Nemo...

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:15.160
Como esta, Senorita Grandis?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:24.880
My dear Nemo, wherever on Earth are you now?

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.330
Wow! King is so high-spirited today.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.790
Is he happy about something?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.250
Nadia!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.290
Come over here, Nadia!

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.250
It's nice and warm here.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.170
That's okay. I don't want to get burned anymore.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.090
What? Is that Grandis?

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.770
What's she doing?

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.390
Stop peeping!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.190
She's throwing letters into the sea.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.070
She loves him so much.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.990
How insensitive!

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.910
Don't you understand the delicate workings of a woman's heart?

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.530
How can I? I'm a boy.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.500
You never even try!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.460
It's delicious!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.920
Don't do that. You'll spoil your dinner.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.510
I won't spoil my dinner. I'm just sampling.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.220
Do you like the taste?

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:58.930
Yes! It's very good! You're just like a real cook!

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:05.140
I am very honored by your praise, young lady.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.860
Say, are you really a rich nobleman, Mr. Ayerton?

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:10.820
Why?

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:15.400
Because you can cook so well, it seems hard to believe.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:19.370
That's because I know the delicious taste of real meals.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:24.330
I partook of so many delicious foods when I was in England.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:29.540
The tastes still lingers on my tongue. That's why I cook so well.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:35.970
I will take you to a grand dinner fit for a princess

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:42.970
when you grow up to be a beautiful young woman.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.150
King!

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.280
A crab.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.400
You've caught a crab, King.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:04.250
How lucky! I can make crab salad now.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.000
Good for you, King!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:13.880
Well, everyone, this is an English lunch I've cooked with great skill.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.050
Please go ahead and try it.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:27.270
Why don't you eat? It's delicious!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.310
I guess so.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.110
Don't mimic me!

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.820
Sanson!
Hanson!

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.530
I can't stand you anymore!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:44.370
I can't put up with you any longer!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.290
A duel!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.370
Wait a minute, you two, don't get so excited.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.790
We can't have any violence here.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.290
How about a race instead?

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:54.550
A race?

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.720
That's right. When you look back at history,

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:02.600
a race was run by representatives of warring countries.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:08.770
That was the origin of the Olympic Games.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.610
Horse racing is a sport for nobles in England.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:18.360
Oh, yes! There's an animal here that we can enter in the race.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.660
But there's only one King.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.490
King is the only one who can beat King.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:29.120
Therefore, you should make your own King, Hanson.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:33.580
Make? Why do I have to do that?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.300
To provide balance.

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:37.250
Balance?

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.380
Right! Sanson, you must train King with your physical power.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:45.720
Hanson, you must make an iron King with your scientific knowledge.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.810
Then make them fight after that.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.350
I see!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.980
You two are both grownups.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:55.310
Don't fight in front of children.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:12:00.360
It's a peaceful way to reach a conclusion, isn't it?

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.340
Good morning, Nadia!

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.920
What are you drinking?

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.090
Just some milk.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.720
Milk?

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.100
Where did you find this goat?

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.600
I found it in the woods.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.190
Don't tell anyone about it.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:39.570
Why not?

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.700
They'll eat it if they find out about it.

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.240
Really?

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.740
That's the way they always are!

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.700
Not always!

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:54.290
If they killed it, they couldn't drink milk anymore.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.920
They really wouldn't eat it?

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.630
What are you doing?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.050
See? It's been smelled out already.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.630
Oh, there's a goat!

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.890
No! It's not for eating.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.970
Did you catch it, Nadia?

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.180
I didn't catch it!

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.020
We became friends.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.480
Right?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:17.690
See?

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.020
Really?

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:22.860
I'll never forgive you if you eat it!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:28.490
Amazing! You can really talk to animals, Nadia.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:33.370
It became possible for me over a period of time.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.090
When I was four or five years old,

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.550
I saw it happen from a circus wagon.

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.890
I saw my friend Smokey taken away.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:58.520
It was because he was considered too old to work.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.900
He left crying out that he didn't want to die.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.830
But I couldn't do a thing.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.290
Since that day,

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.830
I've been able to understand what animals say.

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:19.750
I see.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.420
That's why you can't eat meat?

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:26.300
For everyone else, it's just a matter of food.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:29.090
But to me they are animals being murdered.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.300
Poor Nadia.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:36.270
It can't be helped. You don't understand what animals say.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:40.440
What's wrong, King? Don't you hear me?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.230
King! Run, King!

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.490
Get up, King!

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.910
I'll awaken your wild blood!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:55.490
I want you to dash 100 meters twenty times! Now go!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.710
What's the matter, King? I'll lose if you don't run!

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.840
Wake up! Get up!

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.930
Now, run!

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.900
Please! Just stand up for me!

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:24.570
Please! Just stand up!

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:28.070
My dear King! Please!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.830
Well, I must be a genius to have made this in one night.

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:47.380
This is so fast. The real King won't be able to beat it.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.550
Now, I just have to cover the outside of it.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.640
One color should be Italian red!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.770
Is there something the matter?

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.570
What's wrong with you?

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:11.200
I have something that worries me.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.910
That's why I can't...

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.660
It's not a something, is it?

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.540
It's someone that's troubling your heart.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.340
Right?

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:31.800
Yes, I've been chasing after my love all along.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:34.340
I've been living only for my love, but now it's gone.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:38.060
Love! You must find love for yourself.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.180
It doesn't come to you spontaneously!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.890
You've said it before.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:46.810
We must change our own luck.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:57.120
King?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:06.580
I beg of you! For me! Please!

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:10.880
It's not that easy to make a robot King.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.800
Don't worry about that!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:18.430
Tada! I've stolen these designs from Hanson.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.980
You shouldn't have done that.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:27.230
Look! It has a structural fault.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:28.730
What did you say?

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.940
He needs to get electricity from outside the robot.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:35.900
Can you improve it?

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:39.660
If I could make a small battery, I could build it in.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.030
You can make it, can't you?

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.290
Oh, of course!

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.000
That means I'm going to win!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:49.330
Wait a second! You want to win even through unfair methods?

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:50.590
Yes, I do!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.460
I don't like it.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:56.050
Don't say that. You're my friend, aren't you?

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:00.140
I'll make it if you give a battery to Hanson.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.890
You must fight fair.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.900
No good! It's too heavy!

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:23.700
What's this? These are batteries!

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.160
I can beat Sanson with these!

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.170
I delivered them to him.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.470
It'll be ready soon. See?

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:42.680
This is great! I can win with this!

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:46.850
I used batteries for the joints to make it move smoothly.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.850
Just the outside is left now.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.520
Right! Let's paint it black!

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.360
Black?

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.730
Hanson painted his red.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.780
I also want to put a horn on it.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.990
That will make it heavier.

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.620
But it will also make it look stronger.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.700
Yes! I can win now!

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.500
Men are impossible.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.630
Why is that?

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:17.260
There are lots of things to do, but they just waste time playing.

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:30.770
You're not being fair, Jean. You only helped Sanson.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.320
I'm going to win.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.110
What's that?

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.610
I wonder which will win?

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:43.570
Both of them will fail. At least, that's the way I see it.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.080
Both?

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:49.830
They used the same design. They have the same performance.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.880
Starting from here, make them go around the island.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.250
The first one to arrive will be the winner.

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:59.210
My Black King will win.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:01.550
No! My Red King will!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:04.050
We can't tell until they come back!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.260
I can tell!

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.260
Listen, both of you!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:10.980
You must stop fighting after this race.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:12.810
We know that!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.910
Ready!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.120
Start!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.550
Go!

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:42.590
Beat it!

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:43.720
King!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.260
Darn it! It's too late for him to run!

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.360
Aren't you going to follow them?

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:04.150
They'll come right back here, led by my Black King.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:05.200
Right, Jean?

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.160
Oh, no!

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.120
My Red King

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.700
just runs straight ahead!

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.200
Oh, my!

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:13.580
What's that?

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.000
This is terrible!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.460
My King! My King!

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:18.840
Oh, my goodness!

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.460
Marie's going too!

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.710
Marie! Marie!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.760
This is ridiculous!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.440
Stop! Stop!

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.100
They're not going to stop!

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.360
At the end of this road is...

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:45.150
The ocean!

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:46.700
My invention!

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:48.870
My miniature batteries!

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:52.700
Stop!

00:21:56.580 --> 00:22:00.000
My miniature batteries!

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.220
Stop!

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:09.390
I got them!

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:14.890
What?

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:28.740
Where are the Kings?

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:35.450
Over there.

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:41.750
What?

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:44.460
Where did this come from?

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:06.110
Jean...

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:12.530
What happened to Jean?

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:14.200
How awful.

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:16.950
It's all our own stupid fault.

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:21.540
I would have been kinder if I had known this was going to happen.

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:24.590
Stop it! He hasn't died yet!

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:30.430
Hey!

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:31.090
Jean!

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:32.260
He's alive!

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:33.970
And I was worried!

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:38.350
Hey, Jean!
